-- Castle Nathria (map 2296) -- creature_template downport (05).
-- Source: shadowcore SL-era SQL dumps, transcoded to this fork's 3.3.5 creature_template
-- schema. Priority order per entry: SLDB_902_world_2021_03_12.sql (base dump) overridden
-- column-by-column by 2021_03_18_02_world_cre_gob_data.sql (none of our 148 entries were
-- touched by that file), then the entry-166766 unit_flags/flags_extra fix from
-- 2021_03_18_00_world_darkvein.sql applied last (hand-authored boss-specific correction).
-- All 148 entries had a real source row; nothing had to be defaulted this pass.
--
-- Scope decisions (this pass only):
--   * difficulty_entry_1/2/3 = 0 for ALL rows -- single baseline difficulty tier for now;
--     per-difficulty stat variants are an explicit follow-up, NOT this pass.
--   * minlevel = maxlevel = 80 (flat) for ALL rows, trash and bosses alike -- SL's own
--     level-60 numbering does not translate meaningfully onto this fork's raid-tier
--     convention, so the flat 80 convention used elsewhere for custom raid content is
--     used here instead of preserving the source level. exp = 2 (WotLK stat scaling)
--     and faction = 14 (this fork's hostile-to-all convention for custom raid/area
--     content -- see GiantIsles/giant_water_monster.sql rank=3 boss row and
--     giant_isles_creatures.sql trash rows, both faction=14) are likewise fixed for
--     every row, matching the sibling BlackwingDescent raid's own documented approach
--     of pinning a handful of fields fork-wide rather than trusting the source values.
--   * rank is NOT copied from source -- it is derived strictly from castle_nathria.h's
--     enum Creatures + the actual RegisterCreatureAI(...) bindings read out of the 10
--     boss .cpp files in shadowcore/src/server/scripts/Shadowlands/Revendreth/CastleNathria/:
--     rank=3 for the 13 BossAI-driven encounter-boss entries, rank=1 for the 11
--     ScriptedAI-driven named adds, rank=0 (trash) for the remaining 124 entries --
--     including a handful of entries that ARE individually named in the header enum
--     (e.g. Caramain, Hargitas, Moldovaak, General Draven, the 4 "Container of ..."
--     prop entries) but have no C++ AI class bound to them in this source.
--   * lootid = entry for every row (numeric linkage only; loot table content itself is
--     authored separately, see the loot-focused companion SQL for this raid).
--   * AIName = '' for every row (this fork scripts via ScriptName + SmartAI, not AIName).
--   * ScriptName is set (non-empty) ONLY for the 24 entries below; every other entry is
--     ''. 13 are BossAI encounter bosses (rank 3), 11 are ScriptedAI named adds (rank 1):
--       164261 boss_hungering_destroyer         164406 boss_shriekwing
--       164407 boss_sludgefist                  165066 boss_huntsman_altimor
--       165067 npc_altimor_pet (Margore)         165521 boss_lady_inerva_darkvein
--       165759 boss_sun_kings_salvation          166644 boss_artificer_xymox
--       166969/166970/166971 boss_council_of_blood (Frieda/Stavros/Niklaus)
--       167406 boss_sire_denathrius              168112/168113 boss_stone_legion_generals
--       168156 npc_remornia                      168973 npc_high_torturer_darithos
--       169196 npc_crimson_cabalist               169267 npc_root_of_extinction
--       169457/169458 npc_altimor_pet (Bargast/Hecutis)
--       171577 npc_ripped_soul                    172652 npc_prince_renathal_stone_legion
--       174126/174134 npc_nightcloak (Baron Duskhollow / Lord Evershade)
--     A few entries the original brief expected to be scripted (Shade of Bargast 171557,
--     Fleeting Spirit 168317, Shade of Kael'thas 165805, the 3 "Afterimage of ..." adds,
--     Reverberating Eruption Stalker 175102, Sinister Reflection 170710, Echo of Sin
--     167999, Hand of Destruction 169813) turned out NOT to be among these 148 entries
--     at all once checked against nath_all_cre_ids.txt -- they simply are not in scope
--     for this pass, so no ScriptName was assigned for them here.
--   * creature_template_spell is intentionally skipped this pass -- the source spell ids
--     are Shadowlands spell ids with no equivalent in this 3.3.5 spell_dbc yet (spell/AI
--     porting is a separate later phase), so an empty creature_template_spell is the
--     correct state for now rather than emitting broken spell references.
--   * creature_template_resistance: no non-zero resistance values were found in source
--     for any of these 148 entries, so no rows are emitted for that table either.
--   * 6 `subname` values (165759, 165760, 168112, 172651, 173298, 175232) were
--     double-UTF8-encoded mojibake in the upstream dump (a stray non-breaking space
--     decoded once as Latin-1 and re-encoded); repaired to the intended text here.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- creature_template
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
